    37	     4x5 outline in the output. In the original task, each stray 3-pixel would have stamped the
    38	     teal component around itself; in the combo, the pair jointly determines one whole rectangle.
    39	
    40	b) Complexity calibration:
    41	   - Frames are restricted to a small family of sizes (3x3 up to 5x3 / 3x5 / 4x4). This keeps
    42	     the geometry learnable while still making the hollow-frame change visually obvious.
    43	   - Each source pair must match the learned frame dimensions exactly. That prevents an overly
    44	     permissive "clip any frame into any box" interpretation and makes the fusion visible.
    45	   - Source rectangles are isolated with a one-cell halo, so diagonal pairing is readable and
    46	     accidental alternative pairings are suppressed.
    47	
    48	c) Implicit assumption audit for main():
    49	   - The original main() assumed every non-legend source-colored pixel was an independent source.
    50	     That breaks: markers must be consumed in pairs.
    51	   - The original main() also assumed translation was anchored on one source pixel. That breaks
    52	     too: the relevant geometry is now the full bounding rectangle of a pair, not a single point.
    53	   - The D4 change adds a new assumption: a usable teal component must be a full rectangular
    54	     border of its bbox. The solver filters components accordingly, and the generator guarantees it.
    55	   - Once these assumptions change together, the anchor is used only to associate the correct
    56	     legend pair with the correct teal frame. Placement over non-legend sources comes from the
    57	     recovered rectangle dimensions, not from anchor translation.
    58	
    59	d) Placement legality enforced by the generator:
    60	   - Every non-legend source rectangle contains exactly two colored cells: the diagonal markers.
    61	   - Each source rectangle has the same height/width as that rule's legend frame.
    62	   - Rectangles, legends, teal components, and bystanders are separated by reserved halos so
    63	     nothing overlaps and no false legend can be discovered.
    64	   - Legend teal components are fully in-bounds and isolated under 8-connectivity.
    65	
    66	e) Visual observability:
    67	   - The input shows two strong cues humans can use together: same-color diagonal corner pairs and
    68	     teal empty rectangles in the legend.
    69	   - The output then replaces those corner pairs with colored hollow rectangles of the same size.
    70	     This is visibly different from both the base task and a generic rectangle-filling task.
    71	
    72	f) Visual cleanliness:
    73	   - Output frame bboxes are kept disjoint, so hollow interiors remain legible.
    74	   - Bystanders are excluded from source rectangles and from legend neighborhoods, preventing
    75	     clutter inside empty boxes or near the teaching examples.
    76	
    77	g) Color inference:
    78	   - Color logic is still simple and local: the adjacent legend pair determines the mapping.
    79	     The diagonal markers use only the source color, and the produced frame uses only the target
    80	     color. No extra hidden color categories are introduced.
    81	
    82	h) Generator/solver agreement:
    83	   - The solver assumes valid sources are the only same-color diagonal pairs whose empty bbox
    84	     matches the learned frame dimensions. The generator constructs exactly that family and
    85	     validates each sample by re-running main().
    86	"""
    87	
